{% set arrestDetailsValueHtml %}
<p class="govuk-body">
On police attendance to this incident, PS Bloggs has attended the scene. PC Plod has witnessed two males on the top right corner of the square on Blackford Road. PS Bloggs has approached these males and asked them what had happened, and they replied 'nothing'. A female from an upstairs bedroom at Anywhere STREET has then gestured to and told PS Bloggs that the smaller male pushing a bike who he had just approached was the male who had assaulted Victim. This male has provided his name as Defendant. Defendant has then been arrested by PC Jones.
</p>
<p class="govuk-body">
PS Police has also provided a statement detailing their response to the incident. In their statement they also state that a female from a window on an address on Anywhere STREET has pointed out the suspect to officers and Defendant has then been arrested. In their statement PS Police has also produced images of the victim's injuries, produced as Police Items PP/01 and PP/02. These images show substantial injuries to the victim's face including a foot tread mark, swollen and reddened eyes, lips and cheeks and a bloodies nose.
</p>
{% endset %}

