{% set enquiryValueHtml %}
<ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number govuk-!-margin-bottom-6">
  <li class="govuk-body">
    In this case, it is clear that a motive for the assault existed prior its taking place.
  </li>
  <li class="govuk-body">
    The defendant has, as a result of this incident, filed for divorce from his wife, Helen. She is now a potential witness in this case, and special measures in her regard (video link evidence, etc) will be sought should she be willing to provide evidence. She is of course not compellable as a witness in any case.
  </li>
  <li class="govuk-body">
    In light of the circumstances, the Crown may wish to consider accepting a plea to a lesser charge of wounding without the intention element. While it is the police case that JONES’s selection of a weapon prior to the assault indicates intent to cause GBH, the time element from motivation to assault, along with JONES’ drunken condition, would lend itself to that lesser charge being acceptable.
  </li>
  <li class="govuk-body">
    As indicated in the text of the MG5, no forensic evidence has been sought in respect of JONES’ clothing. The clothing is still available for examination should the Crown consider it necessary, e.g in the light of any proposed defence on JONES’ part.
  </li>
</ol>
{% endset %}

